## Overview

Investigated circulating and urinary microRNAs as non-invasive biomarkers of organ injury in poisoning and toxicological diseases. Using high-throughput molecular techniques and bioinformatics analyses, the project identified novel microRNA signatures associated with kidney injury, poisoning severity, and disease progression.

## Key Achievements

- High-throughput OpenArray RT-qPCR profiling
- Bioinformatics and pathway analyses
- Novel microRNA signature discovery
- Translational biomarker development

## Relevant Publications

- Scientific Reports. 2021
- Archives of Toxicology. 2020
- Toxicology Letters. 2020

## Impact

Established microRNAs as promising early biomarkers for toxicological injuries.
